\par\b\fs28 A2. Connecting hypotheses\b0\fs24\par


\par Hypothesis 1 (one axis): the centre is Source alone \u8212? atonement is God\u8217?s work, the human receives; treatment of the neighbour stays background.\par


\par Hypothesis 2 (relation): the centre is Source \u8596? Coherence \u8212? God gives the atonement (before His face), and that received atonement becomes visible in how we treat the least (Isa. 58 / Matt. 25).\par


\par Which explains the most data with the least strain? Hypothesis 2. It explains why the sanctuary itself is cleansed (sin touches the community), why Isaiah ties fasting to justice, and why Matt. 25 is chosen as the test. Hypothesis 1 leaves the haftarah and the gospel dangling.\par


\par What would refute this reading? If the fruit (the neighbour) were to replace the root (God\u8217?s atonement) \u8212? then it would become works-righteousness, which is exactly what Lev. 16 reverses.\par



