\par\b\fs28 A4. Movement\b0\fs24\par


\par What is unmasked? Religious pride (drawing near as a judge), and form cut off from life \u8212? fasting while you oppress someone, praying while you refuse to forgive; and the anxious holding-on to guilt (your own and another\u8217?s).\par


\par What frame does the text put in its place? Standing before the face of God: He is holy, gives the atonement and carries the guilt away \u8212? and then teaches us to live as people who have received from atonement.\par


\par What concrete response and formation follow? Humble and rest (not saving yourself); bring the form back to justice (Isa. 58); and do not let the least become invisible (Matt. 25) \u8212? including the question: whom must I treat differently because I myself live from atonement?\par


\par \b Core sentence:\b0  Before His face everything falls away but this \u8212? He is holy, He carries the guilt away; and whoever receives that can no longer let the other stay invisible.\par


\par \b Horizon (ground, not the week\u8217?s theme):\b0  Yeshua, the High Priest who by His own blood appears \u8220?in the presence of God for us\u8221? (Heb. 9\u8211?10) \u8212? the pattern points, it does not flatten Leviticus 16.\par


